{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] says: regarding the raqia, things that did not [previously] exist. Rather, its meaning is something spread out, like “and they hammered out” (Exodus 39:3), “I would beat them” (2 Samuel 22:43), and likewise “and stretches them out like a tent to dwell in” (Isaiah 40:22). How weighty is the saying of one who says that the ends of heaven [n] together with the ends of the waters of the Ocean — and this raqia is the air, for when the light grew strong over the earth and a dry wind from the earth, the heat was transformed and the raqia was made. And likewise he said in the psalm (Psalm 104:2), “who stretches out the heavens like a curtain,” covering with water, and he mentioned the clouds and the wind, and founded the earth, and it is high above the waters, and likewise he wrote, “for He founded it upon seas” (Psalm 24:2), “to Him who spread the earth upon the waters” (Psalm 136:6). And likewise everyone who goes toward the sea is called descending, and the meaning of “who calls for the waters of the sea” (Amos 5:8, 9:6) is that they rise, and they are the clouds, and afterward he pours them out."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra quotes Saadia as rejecting creation ex nihilo for the raqia; the syntax of the Gaon's position is compressed and difficult. The text reads השמש (the sun), a known copyist error for השמים (the heavens), here corrected silently per the editor's צ\"ל notation. The clause beginning 'How weighty' (ומה נכבד) appears to introduce a physical description that Ibn Ezra endorses or attributes to Saadia; the transition is abrupt in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:35.853388532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}